      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The hamlet’s name comes from the Oneida word for “place of wild plums,” echoing the river that gives the town its name.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.townofotselic.org/town-information",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In the 1800s South Otselic boasted an opera house, a rope‑and‑line factory, and two hotels, showing how lively the community once was.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.townofotselic.org/town-information",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The New York, Oswego & Midland Railroad, nicknamed the Butter & Cheese Express, once ran through Otselic, linking the town to regional markets.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://chenangohistorical.org/town/otselic/",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "South Otselic hosts a New York State Fish Hatchery, a legacy of the area’s long fishing heritage.",
